  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "The development to which this permission relates shall be carried out in accordance with the materials specified on the approved plans and on the submitted application form unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning authority.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development, in accordance with Policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The works shall be carried out and maintained in accordance with the deposited Reasonable Exception Statement  compliant with Policy D12(A).\r\rReason: In the interests of fire safety and to ensure the safety of all building users in accordance with Policy D12 (Fire Safety) of the London Plan 2021.\r",
    "No gate shall open over the highway (for the avoidance of doubt the highway includes the pavement).\r\rReason : in the interests of the safety and operation of the highway network, in accordance with policies T4 and T7 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies CS7 and DM9 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012. \r",
    "Electronic gate condition \rThe gates hereby approved shall open into the application site and not on the public highway and shall only be electronically operated. \r\rReason: To ensure highway safety in accordance with Policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.\r\r",
    "The main vehicular main gate and the pedestrian side gate hereby approved shall remain permeable. No solid backing should be installed to ensure visibility in and out of the site. \r\rReason: To ensure highway safety in accordance with Policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.\r\r"
  ],
